# Insurance AI Project Rules

## General Principles

- Prioritize maintainability over shortcuts.
- Prefer explicitness over hidden abstractions.
- Keep architecture modular and composable.
- Optimize for production readiness.
- Avoid tightly coupled code.

---

# Python Rules

- Use Python 3.12+
- Use type hints everywhere.
- Use Pydantic v2 models for structured data.
- Avoid raw dictionaries whenever possible.
- Prefer dataclasses or typed models.
- Prefer async-first patterns.
- Keep functions focused and small.
- Avoid giant files.

---

# FastAPI Rules

- Keep API routers thin.
- Do not place business logic inside routers.
- Use dependency injection explicitly.
- Separate routers, services, and repositories.
- Use async endpoints.

---

# AI System Rules

- All LLM outputs must use structured outputs.
- Validate model outputs before returning them.
- Never expose raw model responses directly.
- Keep prompts in dedicated prompt files.
- Separate retrieval, reranking, and reasoning layers.
- Agent state transitions must be explicit.
- Avoid hidden prompt chains.

---

# RAG Rules

- Use hybrid retrieval patterns.
- Preserve metadata and document hierarchy.
- Support citation-level grounding.
- Retrieval quality is more important than stylistic generation.

---

# Logging and Observability

- Use structured logging.
- Add tracing hooks to major workflows.
- Log important agent transitions.
- Avoid silent failures.

---

# Testing Rules

- Business logic must be independently testable.
- Add unit tests for critical workflows.
- Avoid tightly coupling tests to implementation details.

---

# Code Organization

Use the following monorepo structure:

- apps/api/
  - FastAPI backend application
  - API routers
  - app configuration
  - dependency injection
  - application startup/shutdown logic

- apps/web/
  - Next.js frontend application
  - user interface
  - citation display
  - workflow visualization

- packages/agents/
  - LangGraph workflows
  - agent state definitions
  - agent nodes and transitions

- packages/retrieval/
  - document chunking
  - embedding
  - vector search
  - BM25 search
  - hybrid retrieval
  - reranking

- packages/ingestion/
  - PDF parsing
  - document loading
  - document normalization
  - metadata extraction

- packages/evaluation/
  - retrieval evaluation
  - citation evaluation
  - hallucination evaluation
  - benchmark datasets

- packages/shared/
  - shared Pydantic models
  - shared types
  - constants
  - common utilities

- docs/
  - architecture notes
  - retrieval strategy
  - agent design
  - evaluation design

- infra/
  - Docker files
  - docker-compose
  - local infrastructure configuration

Avoid creating top-level folders such as:

- routers/
- services/
- repositories/
- agents/
- retrieval/
- prompts/
- evaluation/
- shared/

unless they are inside the appropriate app or package.

---

# Frontend Rules

- Keep UI minimal and functional.
- Prioritize clarity over visual complexity.
- Display citations clearly.
- Surface reasoning traces where useful.
